==English==
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pleh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|accomplisshen}}, {{m|enm|acomplissen}}, from {{der|en|fro||acompliss-}}, extended stem of {{m|fro|acomplir}} (Modern French {{m|fr|accomplir}}),<ref>{{R:MED Online|accomplisshen|v|MED286|20 October 2019|date=2018}}</ref> from {{der|en|VL.||*(ac)complīre}}, from {{der|en|la|compleo|complēre|t=fill up/out, complete|pos=whence English {{m|en|complete}}}}.

First attested in the late 14th century.

